; A balance assertion or assignment is computed as of its posting's date.
; When that date is written as `[DATE]` in the posting's note, after the
; amount, the parser must read it before computing the balance, so that
; the 2021/03/15 deposit (dated after both) is left out: the assertion
; sees 12 r, and the assignment, dated 2021/03/02, posts 20 r - 12 r.

2021/01/01 Opening
    Assets:Bank                       10 r
    Equity:Opening

2021/03/15 Deposit
    Assets:Bank                        5 r
    Income:Salary

2021/04/01 Reconcile
    Assets:Bank                        2 r = 12 r ; [2021/03/01]
    Income:Interest

2021/04/02 Adjust
    Assets:Bank                            = 20 r ; [2021/03/02]
    Equity:Adjustment

test bal Assets
                25 r  Assets:Bank
end test

test reg Assets --sort date
21-Jan-01 Opening               Assets:Bank                    10 r         10 r
21-Mar-01 Reconcile             Assets:Bank                     2 r         12 r
21-Mar-02 Adjust                Assets:Bank                     8 r         20 r
21-Mar-15 Deposit               Assets:Bank                     5 r         25 r
end test
